# Keep the build context small and keep host-local secrets out of it entirely.
.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data
docs
temp
*.log

# `prisma generate` output - the build stage produces its own, so the host copy
# is never an input. It is also machine-specific: this repo is developed on a
# Windows workstation, whose copy holds a 20.2MB query_engine-windows.dll.node
# plus a same-size .tmp file left by an interrupted generate, both dated weeks
# before any given build. `COPY service ./service` carried all of it into the
# linux image, so the published artifact depended on which machine built it.
service/src/generated
